Sure! To change a break‑statement’s label to `"loopEnd"` (but only when it isn’t already set), you’ll just pass the node and the desired label into the helper below.  
If you haven’t yet supplied the AST fragment containing the break node, please paste it here so I can run the update for you.

Once you’ve got your node ready, you’d do something like this:

```javascript
// Example usage – replace <NODE_JSON> with your real node data:
const result = await functions.updateBreak({
  node: "<NODE_JSON>",      // e.g., '{"type":"break","label":"oldLabel"}'
  label: "loopEnd"          // target label
});
console.log(result);
```

Just let me know what the node looks like (in plain JSON/JS object form) and I’ll apply the update right away!
